{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "בשטים", :translit "b'shitim", :gloss "in Shittim"} {:he "כי תשטה אשתו", :translit "ki tisteh ishto", :gloss "when his wife goes astray"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name בשטים read as from root שטה, 'to go astray,' as in Numbers 5:12 כי תשטה אשתו"}], :frame {:text "Numbers 5:12 uses the root שטה for a wife 'going astray' (תשטה), the same root underlying the place-name Shittim. The Ba'al HaTurim reads the location-name itself as an allusion to the Israelites' sexual going astray that begins here in Numbers 25:1.", :sources ["Numbers 5:12" "Numbers 25:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ויחל העם", :translit "vayehel ha-am", :gloss "and the people began"} {:he "רבים חללים", :translit "rabim chalalim", :gloss "many slain/corpses"} {:he "באשה זרה", :translit "b'ishah zarah", :gloss "with a strange woman"} {:he "ע\"ז", :translit "avodah zarah", :gloss "idolatry (abbreviated)"} {:he "זה שטים", :translit "zeh shitim", :gloss "this is Shittim"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "ויחל read as from root חלל — both 'began' and 'profaned' — producing phrase רבים חללים"} {:kind :gematria, :a "באשה זרה", :b "זה שטים"}], :frame {:text "Proverbs repeatedly uses אשה זרה ('strange woman') as a figure for sexual temptation, and rabbinic tradition in sources such as Masekhet Avodah Zarah 8a identifies idolatry with the seductive 'strange woman.' The Ba'al HaTurim links this dual meaning to Numbers 25:1–2, where Israel's sin at Shittim encompassed both immorality and idolatry.", :sources ["Proverbs 2:16" "Proverbs 5:3" "Proverbs 7:5" "Avodah Zarah 8a" "Numbers 25:1-2"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Place-name בשטים read as from root שטה, 'to go astray,' as in Numbers 5:12 כי תשטה אשתו", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "ויחל read as from root חלל — both 'began' and 'profaned' — producing phrase רבים חללים", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "באשה זרה", :a-value 520, :b "זה שטים", :b-value 371, :len